    {
      "id": "3d051e10-6d6a-4678-8233-3dd421c14a23",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 752,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## Scheduled Risk Data Intake\nThis section starts the workflow on a daily schedule and immediately pulls active client records, recent checkins, and recent weekly form submissions from Supabase. It prepares all core activity data in one place so the workflow can evaluate engagement patterns and identify inactive clients without manual effort."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a5d425fe-6c7d-48d8-9f43-218b2b9db3c6",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        800,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## Risk Analysis Engine\n\nThis section consolidates client activity data and performs the core risk analysis. It merges datasets, calculates inactivity metrics, weekly checkin counts, missed forms, and risk scores, then filters only high-risk clients requiring coach attention or re-engagement outreach.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "28af0bc3-26f3-402e-93fb-8296d32487b2",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2288,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## AI Draft Generation\nThis section creates the personalized re engagement message using Gemini and then converts the model output into usable workflow fields. It ensures the generated response becomes a clean subject and message body that can be reused across Slack notifications, Gmail outreach, and event logging.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ce96f183-209a-49fa-b950-3a4827544c1f",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1648,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 592,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## Alert Preparation and Control\nThis section prevents duplicate alerts through cooldown checks and prepares structured data for notifications. It validates timing constraints, formats Slack summaries, AI prompt context, escalation labels, and detection timestamps so downstream communication nodes receive clean, reusable alert fields.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3acd2795-4aa9-44bc-ac7b-63aea4166268",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4064,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 576,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## Client Status Sync\nThis section updates the client master records after the alert has been processed. It stores the latest alert timestamp, message timestamp, escalation level, and risk state so the next workflow run uses fresh status information and stays aligned across Supabase and Google Sheets.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "88feb551-1c8d-40f7-a9c1-2bd297843753",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2976,
        -48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 656,
        "content": "## Coach and Client Communication\nThis section handles the external communication triggered by detected risk cases. It sends a coach facing risk alert to Slack and an automated re engagement email to the client through Gmail, ensuring both internal visibility and client outreach happen as part of the same workflow run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e1ef5731-5671-4add-8ab1-d994b4c4ccea",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3504,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 512,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## Risk Logging\nThis section records every triggered risk event in both Supabase and Google Sheets for audit and reporting purposes. It helps maintain a durable history of alerts, message content, and escalation state while also keeping a visible reporting layer available for operational review and handoff.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "aa34a4c9-ce8b-4812-8176-460e90227ed5",
      "name": "Sticky Note7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -736,
        -64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 688,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## How workflow works\nThis workflow automatically detects gym clients who may be disengaging based on missed checkins and missing weekly form submissions. It begins with a schedule trigger, then loads active clients, recent checkins, and recent weekly form activity from Supabase. After merging the datasets, a Code node calculates risk score, inactivity days, missed activity counts, and escalation logic for each client. Only high priority clients move forward, and a cooldown check prevents duplicate alerts within a defined period. The workflow then prepares context for Gemini, generates a supportive re engagement draft, and parses the AI output into structured subject and message fields. Finally, it sends alerts to Slack and Gmail, logs the risk event in Supabase and Google Sheets, and updates client status records in both systems for future workflow runs.\n\n## Setup Steps\n1. Configure the schedule trigger to run daily at your preferred monitoring time in India timezone.\n2. Connect Supabase credentials and confirm the clients, checkins, weekly_forms, and risk_events tables are available.\n3. Connect Google Sheets credentials and map the Clients_Master and Risk_Alert_Log sheets correctly.\n4. Connect Gemini credentials and test the AI node to confirm it returns valid JSON with subject and body.\n5. Connect Slack and Gmail credentials and verify both notification nodes send test messages successfully.\n6. Rename nodes using the final naming list and place sticky notes above each section with the provided section titles and descriptions.\n7. Run the workflow with sample client data, confirm the logging and status update steps work correctly, then publish the final validated version.  \n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
